        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of figured satin and woven silk. Woven in cream and red on a black ground are patterns inspired by Japanese designs. They are arranged in triangles which form four squares in the width of the material. There is more cream silk in some of the triangles, and red in the other triangles, forming large diamond or lozenge patterns."@en , "Furnishing fabric 'Yesso' of silk and satin, designed by Bruce James Talbert, made by Warner and Sons, Spitalfields, 1870"@en ;
